      "text_raw": "The only difference between\nthe previous amplifier and\nthis one is the use of a cur-\nrent mirror as a second\nstage. The input and output\nstage are the same. Also the\nload capacitance and the\ncurrents are the same.\nThe only question is\ntherefore, which one of these\namplifiers can achieve a\nhigher GBW. This will obvi-\nously depend on the non-\ndominant poles associated\nwith the second stage.\nThis amplifier is denoted\nby a ‘‘nested Miller’’ although both of them are nested Miller amplifiers.",
